CHAPTER III
SCOPE
Article 5
The scope of protection of women and children from violence is as follows:
a. forms of violence against women and children;
b. rights of victims;
c. obligations and responsibilities;
d. implementation of protection of women and children from violence;
e. institutions;
f. cooperation and partnership;
g. monitoring and evaluation;
h. reporting;
i. funding; and
j. sanctions.

Article 35
(1) In order to achieve the objectives of protection of women and children as referred to in Article 4, the Regional Government may cooperate with:
a. the Government;
b. other Regional Governments; and/or
c. non-governmental institutions.
(2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1), includes:
a. exchange of data and information;
b. rehabilitation of victims of acts of violence;
c. repatriation and social reintegration;
d. provision of evidence and witnesses; and
e. empowerment.
(3) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) and paragraph (2) shall be set forth in the form of a Joint Agreement and/or Cooperation Agreement in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.

Article 10
The obligations and responsibilities in the implementation of protection for women and children from violence are the shared responsibility of:
a. Regional Government;
b. Village Government;
c. Community; and
d. Parents, Guardians and/or Family.

Article 16
(1) Prevention as referred to in Article 15 letter a, shall be implemented by means of:
a. forming a working network in efforts to prevent violence;
b. conducting coordination, integration, synchronization of violence prevention based on partnership patterns;
c. establishing a violence prevention system;
d. conducting socialization regarding laws and regulations related to the protection of women and children victims of violence; and
e. providing knowledge about prevention and mechanisms for handling violence against women and children.
(2) Prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be implemented in an integrated manner by Regional Apparatus of the Regency and related agencies whose main duties and functions are in the fields of:
a. women's empowerment and child protection;
b. education;
c. health;
d. social affairs;
e. manpower;
f. youth and sports; and
g. mental and spiritual.
(3) In addition to being implemented by Regional Apparatus of the Regency and related agencies as referred to in paragraph (2), prevention shall also be implemented by:
a. family and/or closest relatives;
b. community, NGOs, community organizations, social organizations and religious organizations; and
c. business sector.

Article 4
The objectives of protection of women and children from violence are: a. to prevent violence against women and children;
b. to eliminate all forms of violence against women and children; c. to protect and provide a sense of security for women and children; d. to provide services to women and children victims of violence;
e. to carry out rehabilitation and reintegration of women and children victims of violence; and
f. to carry out empowerment of women and children victims of violence.

Article 34
(1) The Village/Urban Village Level Women and Children Protection Task Force as referred to in Article 31 letter c, constitutes a functional work unit that provides integrated protection services and handling of cases of violence against children and women at the Village/Urban Village level.
(2) The Management of the Village/Urban Village Level Women and Children Protection Task Force as referred to in paragraph (1) consists of:
a. elements of Village/Urban Village apparatus;
b. elements of Village/Urban Village Guidance Non-Commissioned Officers (Babinsa);
c. elements of Community Guidance Non-Commissioned Officers (Babinmas);
d. community leaders/religious leaders;
e. youth elements; and
f. elements of the Village/Urban Village PKK Mobilization Team.
(3) The main duties of the Village/Urban Village Level Women and Children Protection Task Force as referred to in paragraph (1) are:
a. providing services in the context of protection of women and children;
b. receiving community complaints regarding cases of violence against women and children in the Village/Urban Village area;
c. facilitating women and children who are victims of violence in resolving their problems;
d. conducting outreach to the community regarding the protection of women and children; and
e. providing assistance to victims or referring them to the Sub-District level women and children protection task group.
(4) Further provisions regarding the establishment, duties and functions of the Village/Urban Village Level Women and Children Protection Task Force as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be stipulated by Decree of the Village Head/Urban Village Head (Lurah).

Article 33
(1) The Sub-District Level Task Force for the Protection of Women and Children as referred to in Article 31 letter b, constitutes a functional work unit that provides integrated protection services and handling of cases of violence against children and women at the Sub-District level.
(2) The members/personnel of the Sub-District Level Task Force for the Protection of Women and Children as referred to in paragraph (1) consist of:
a. elements of the Sub-District apparatus;
b. agencies/institutions at the Sub-District level;
c. elements of the Sector Police (Polsek);
d. elements of the Military District Command (Koramil);
e. community leaders/religious leaders;
f. youth elements; and
g. elements of the Sub-District PKK Driving Team.
(3) The main duties of the Sub-District Level Task Force for the Protection of Women and Children as referred to in paragraph (1) are:
a. providing services in the context of protecting women and children;
b. receiving public complaints regarding cases of violence against women and children in the Sub-District and Urban Village/Village areas;
c. facilitating women and children who are victims of violence in resolving their problems;
d. disseminating information to the community about the protection of women and children; and
e. providing assistance for victims or referring them to P2TP2A, Sector Police (Polsek)/Resort Police (Polres), hospitals or other institutions as required.
(4) Further provisions regarding the formation, duties, and functions of the Sub-District Level Task Force for the Protection of Women and Children as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be stipulated by a Decision of the Sub-District Head.

Article 19
Forms of services for victims as referred to in Article 17 letter b, consist of:
a. services for women and children victims of acts of violence, including:
1. complaint, consultation and counseling services;
2. assistance services;
3. health services;
4. legal aid services; and
5. repatriation and social reintegration services.
b. special services for women victims of acts of domestic violence or human trafficking, including:
1. complaint services;
2. pick-up services;
3. medical and psychological referral services;
4. shelter services;
5. assistance and legal aid services; and
6. repatriation and social reintegration services.

CHAPTER IV
FORMS OF VIOLENCE AGAINST WOMEN AND CHILDREN
Article 6
Forms of violence against women and children, among others:
a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. neglect;
e. exploitation; and/or
f. other violence.

CHAPTER II
PRINCIPLES, PURPOSE AND OBJECTIVES
Article 2
Protection of women and children from violence is based on the principles of: a. humanity;
b. justice and gender equality;
c. protection;
d. best interests of women and children; and
e. non-discrimination.

CHAPTER V
RIGHTS OF VICTIMS
Article 8
